CORE
main.c
--pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 18 p is target or NULL: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 20 dereference failure: pointer NULL in \*p: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 25 q is NULL: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 31 dereference failure: pointer NULL in \*r: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 34 dereference failure: pointer NULL in \*p: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[.*\] line ([0-9]|[12][0-9]|3[0-3]) .*: FAILURE$
^warning: ignoring
--
Pointers read back from the bytes of an untyped object: zero bytes must be
treated as a null pointer, which pointer checks still flag when dereferenced,
while bytes of a valid pointer must still yield that pointer.
